    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics feels both daunting and fascinating—like a puzzle wrapped in abstract logic. My parents’ education backgrounds (one with a master’s in STEM, the other vocational) made me aware of its power but also created anxiety around complexity. I enjoy problem-solving, but when it gets too technical, my neuroticism kicks in. Still, I return to it because structure and precision have always felt grounding.",
